 "crosscheck": "Each Earth reference is checked against an adaptive DOP853 integration of the continuous profile, restarted at every density jump, run to the double-precision limit.  That check is itself double precision and follows the reference only to about 9e-12; the limit is the check's, not the reference's.  What confirms it beneath that is a second extrapolation at full precision sharing no slab count with the first: at three flavors two disjoint 50-digit ladders, (32..1024) and (48..768), agree to 1.1e-16.  The 3+1 referee is the coarser construction, a single Richardson pair rather than a ladder, and the disjoint pair (768, 1536) confirms it to 1.2e-12.",
